---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, issuesUrl } from "../config/site";
const updated = new Date(site.legalUpdated).toLocaleDateString("en", { year: "numeric", month: "long", day: "numeric" });
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What this website does and doesn't collect.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>reinvent-the-wheel.com is a static website. It has no accounts, no forms, and no comments.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>No cookies</strong> are set by this website.</li>
        <li><strong>No analytics or tracking scripts</strong> are used.</li>
        <li><strong>No third-party requests:</strong> fonts, scripts and images are served from this domain.</li>
        <li><strong>Theme preference:</strong> if you switch between light and dark, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage on your device. It's never sent anywhere. Clearing your site data removes it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/">Cloudflare</a>. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes technical request data —
        such as IP addresses, browser information and requested pages — to deliver and protect the site. See
        <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>. The project doesn't add analytics on top of that.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>Links to GitHub, content publishers and other projects take you to sites with their own privacy practices.</p>

      <h2>The RTW software</h2>
      <p>
        This page covers the website only. The RTW software runs on your own devices and contains no telemetry. It connects to the internet only when
        you ask it to — installing (package managers, GitHub, Kiwix, the npm registry) and fetching content from the publishers listed in the
        documentation. Readers who use your library talk only to your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>{issuesUrl ? <>Open an issue on <a href={issuesUrl}>GitHub</a>.</> : "Contact the maintainer through the project repository."}</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
